<%- include('layout-start.ejs', { title: 'Control — PanelsDCC Manual', basePath, activeNav: 'getting-started' }) %>
<div class="main-container">
    <div class="getting-started-layout">
        <%- include('sidebar-docs.ejs', { basePath, manualChapter: 3 }) %>
        <div class="getting-started-layout-main">
            <div class="full-width-section">
                <div class="section-text">
                    <h1>Chapter 3 — Control</h1>
                    <p>PanelsDCC Control is the operator interface for your layout: driving trains, operating accessories, and using panels. Complete getting started through <a href="<%= basePath %>/getting-started/first-train.html">§1.4 Driving your first train</a> and <a href="<%= basePath %>/getting-started/account.html">§1.5 Your PanelsDCC account</a> if you have not verified a local run and sign-in path yet.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <hr/>
            <div class="full-width-section" id="trains">
                <div class="section-text">
                    <h2>Trains</h2>
                    <p>Operation is built around clear speed, direction, and function feedback. With an account, your configured locomotives and function maps sync from the cloud; without login you can still select by DCC address for testing.</p>
                    <p>Use the train list or panel overlays to drive; status at the top of the screen reflects connection state to Connect.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <hr/>
            <div class="full-width-section" id="accessories">
                <div class="section-text">
                    <h2>Accessories</h2>
                    <p>Points, signals, and other accessories appear with live state where your layout and configuration define them. Route and macro behaviour depends on <a href="<%= basePath %>/configuration/index.html">Configuration</a>.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <hr/>
            <div class="full-width-section" id="panels">
                <div class="section-text">
                    <h2>Panels</h2>
                    <p>Graphical panels mirror your track and signalling. Operate routes and overlays from a single view where you have configured panels.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <hr/>
            <div class="full-width-section">
                <div class="section-text">
                    <h2>More detail</h2>
                    <p>For PWA installation, login behaviour, connection status, and quick test by DCC number, see <a href="<%= basePath %>/getting-started/first-train.html">Getting started — Driving your first train</a> and expand your workflow using the rest of this chapter as reference.</p>
                    <p>For layout design, see <a href="<%= basePath %>/configuration/index.html">Chapter 2 — Configuration</a>. For profile, sync, Wi‑Fi, and updates, see <a href="<%= basePath %>/system-admin/index.html">Chapter 4 — System admin</a>.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<%- include('layout-end.ejs') %>
